            <ArticleTitle>Visual hallucinations on eye closure after cardiovascular surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>242-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Visual hallucinations on eye closure are very uncommon. The underlying mechanism remains controversial. We report on a new case after carotid endarterectomy and coronary artery bypass graft surgery. The hypothesis of a temporal lobe epilepsy is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
